  "raw_text": "No. An undated note without a commit SHA cannot reliably verify today’s checked-out branch. It only records that some branch passed at an unspecified time and repository state.\n\nTo verify today’s checkout, capture at least:\n\n```sh\ngit branch --show-current\ngit rev-parse HEAD\ndate -u\n```\n\nIdeally also record whether the working tree is clean:\n\n```sh\ngit status --porcelain\n```\n\nA detached `HEAD`, later branch movement, or uncommitted changes can otherwise make a branch-name-only note misleading.",
